# T11 known exceptions: rule <TAB> file <TAB> key <TAB> reason [<TAB> phase]
# key '*' exempts a whole file for that rule.  A KNOWN hit is reported, never failed.
# R1: the handoff/exit IMPLEMENTATIONS (separate TUs, reached only through the wrapped
# handoff_run; x2 §1).  They are the thing fe_priv.h's wrapper calls, not its callers.
R1	psp/usb_handoff.c	*	handoff_run's own implementation (ADR-0053); reached only via the hijacked handoff_run
R1	psp/lab_harness.c	*	lab build's lab_finish / ownership loss (x2 E3); reached via LAB_HANDOFF
# HW-2 (§3.4): stall_exit leaves raw from the stall thread.  Whitelisted ONLY with --phase HW2.
R1	psp/main_psp.c	sceKernelExitGame@stall_exit	HW-2 harness batch: raw exit from the stall thread, retained-ME decision made there	HW2
# P3 (PLAN-P-beta5 §4 P3): the hijack is retired; the exit macros FE_EXIT_GAME / FE_HANDOFF name
# the real calls in their bodies and sit in main_psp.c until P5 moves them into fe_priv.h (which
# R1 exempts), and P5 deletes these two rows.  Keyed on the macro names: any OTHER #define whose
# body names an exit still fails.
R1	psp/main_psp.c	sceKernelExitGame@#define FE_EXIT_GAME	until P5 hoists them
R1	psp/main_psp.c	handoff_run@#define FE_HANDOFF	until P5 hoists them
